  THE CONVENTIONS, DECLARED, and one correction to the pin's own
  suggested pattern, made in place.  The pin proposes 'the
  committed one, plus a second — e.g. the D57 S4 pattern of a
  maximally coarse terminal'.  But the COMMITTED terminal IS
  already the maximally coarse one: G(h, 0) = 1 is
  state-independent, it gives every terminal history the same
  value, and there is nothing coarser.  The S4 pattern therefore
  INVERTS here: a second convention has to REFINE the terminal,
  not coarsen it.  Two are declared and both are carried
  independently through the whole computation:
    C1 (COMMITTED, D46b): G(h, 0) = 1.  Maximally coarse.
    C2 (BRANCH-COUNT TERMINAL): G(h, 0) = |menu(h)|, the number
       of admissible continuations.  Counting measure at the
       cap layer instead of uniform measure — a genuinely
       different completion of the truncation, and NOT a
       reparametrization of C1.
    C3 (MENU-MASS TERMINAL): G(h, 0) = sum_e q(e|h).  DECLARED
       AND GATED TO BE A HORIZON SHIFT of C1 — it can never
       separate, and it is carried precisely so that C2's
       separation cannot be mistaken for one.
